course: dictionary
lesson: 2692
title: Differ: not the same, or not agreeing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To differ means to be not the same as something else. «Your dose differs from your little sister's» tells you your amount is not hers, because your age and weight are not the same. Look for the words around differ, like «from» or «by», and they will help you.
explain: The word can also mean to have a different opinion. «We differ on which film is best» means you and your friend do not agree about the film. You can still be friends. The phrase «agree to differ» means you accept that you disagree, and you both stay friendly.
explain: In maths, differ tells you how far apart two numbers are. If two numbers differ by 5, one is 5 more than the other. Try it: swap your meaning into the sentence. «Brothers and sisters differ» still makes sense if you think "are not the same", so you have the right meaning.
fact: To differ means to be not the same as something else.
fact: To differ can also mean to disagree, to have a different opinion.
fact: «Differ by 5» means the gap between two numbers is 5.
fact: «Agree to differ» means you accept that you disagree and stay friendly.
fact: Different words can share a sound: «differ» and «different» are related, but a word like «bare» means something else.
exercise: «Your dose differs from your little sister's.» What does differs mean here? | Is taken away from | *Is not the same as | Is bigger than the moon | Is exactly the same as
exercise: «The two numbers differ by 5.» What does this tell you? | They are both 5 | *They are 5 apart | They are both zero | They add up to 5
exercise: «We differ on which film is best.» What does differ mean here? | Agree completely | *Have different opinions | Watch films together | Are the same age
test: «The British say "at the weekend", but Americans say "on the weekend", so countries differ.» What does differ mean here? | Are exactly alike | Are close friends | Are very cold | *Are not the same
test: Ella and Sam differ in opinion, but they stay friends. What does «agree to differ» mean? | Agree on everything | Win the argument | *Accept you disagree and stay friendly | Never speak to each other again
exam: «The two prices differ by 5 pounds.» What does «by 5 pounds» tell you? | Each price is 5 pounds | *The gap between the prices is 5 pounds | Both prices are free | The prices add up to 5 pounds
